1
00:00:14,740 --> 00:00:18,270
♪I stretch and yawn
when the sun is high in the sky♪

2
00:00:19,170 --> 00:00:23,030
♪A cup of tea and a little tune,
what a carefree life♪

3
00:00:23,890 --> 00:00:28,480
♪The fortune teller said
love would come my way this year♪

4
00:00:28,740 --> 00:00:32,580
♪But all I see is my food
arriving right on time♪

5
00:00:33,850 --> 00:00:35,670
♪No rush, no worries♪

6
00:00:35,670 --> 00:00:38,360
♪Love is all a matter of chance♪

7
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:40,480
♪Flowers bloom and fade♪

8
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:43,380
♪I'd rather take good care
of myself first♪

9
00:00:43,380 --> 00:00:45,580
♪Two orioles sing among
the green willows♪

10
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:47,970
♪And I still don't have a boyfriend♪

11
00:00:48,180 --> 00:00:50,590
♪My best years are nothing
to worry about♪

12
00:00:50,590 --> 00:00:53,240
♪I'll stay happily single
till I'm old and gray♪

13
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:07,540
=Besties' Coming Fortune=

14
00:01:07,580 --> 00:01:09,980
=Episode 9=

15
00:01:44,350 --> 00:01:44,920
This

16
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:48,870
is where I want to be.

17
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:03,920
Well, yes, but...

18
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:08,280
How should I put this?

19
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:09,630
I think my injury

20
00:02:09,630 --> 00:02:10,550
is a bit more urgent

21
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:12,390
than what's happening between you two.

22
00:02:16,750 --> 00:02:17,320
Wow.

23
00:02:19,080 --> 00:02:19,510
Wow.

24
00:02:20,120 --> 00:02:21,950
Am I interrupting something?

25
00:02:23,240 --> 00:02:24,230
Oh, stop it.

26
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:25,790
He kissed me first.

27
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:28,870
He made the first move.

28
00:02:28,870 --> 00:02:30,110
But let me ask you something.

29
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:33,160
Is that really a sword wound?

30
00:02:34,870 --> 00:02:36,140
Of course it is.

31
00:02:38,430 --> 00:02:40,080
Fate made him my younger brother.

32
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:41,670
Protecting him

33
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:43,440
is my destiny.

34
00:02:44,390 --> 00:02:45,560
Shutiao,

35
00:02:46,870 --> 00:02:47,880
do you believe in fate?

36
00:02:48,870 --> 00:02:49,880
Why ask me that all of a sudden?

37
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:50,950
Are you trying to sell me a course?

38
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:52,760
No.

39
00:02:54,680 --> 00:02:55,520
I was just thinking

40
00:02:55,520 --> 00:02:57,360
the original heroines
should be returning soon.

41
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,390
Once the story gets back on track,

42
00:03:00,630 --> 00:03:02,080
we'll have to leave quickly.

43
00:03:02,840 --> 00:03:03,510
So,

44
00:03:03,630 --> 00:03:04,470
before we go, I want to

45
00:03:04,470 --> 00:03:05,760
cure Shen Cheng of his poisoning.

46
00:03:07,240 --> 00:03:08,240
But the antidote

47
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:09,480
still needs one final ingredient.

48
00:03:09,910 --> 00:03:11,160
What was it called again?

49
00:03:12,080 --> 00:03:12,710
Immortal Heart Herb.

50
00:03:13,060 --> 00:03:14,340
Immortal Heart Herb?

51
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:18,800
When I was interning at
a traditional Chinese medicine hospital,

52
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:20,160
I think the director mentioned it.

53
00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:22,680
He said this herb is not only
hard to find,

54
00:03:22,810 --> 00:03:23,680
but even harder to preserve.

55
00:03:23,940 --> 00:03:25,710
Its medicinal properties
fade within half an hour.

56
00:03:25,910 --> 00:03:27,080
Modern laboratories

57
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:28,110
can preserve it at low temperatures,

58
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:29,920
but we don't have that option here.

59
00:03:30,010 --> 00:03:31,010
Then what should we do?

60
00:03:33,190 --> 00:03:33,790
Let me think.

61
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:39,560
We could use wild chrysanthemum

62
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:40,710
and mint as substitutes.

63
00:03:40,870 --> 00:03:41,880
Wild chrysanthemum cools the blood,

64
00:03:42,080 --> 00:03:43,520
while mint clears heat
and removes toxins.

65
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:44,790
When combined,

66
00:03:45,080 --> 00:03:46,710
they can work just as well
as Immortal Heart Herb.

67
00:03:47,310 --> 00:03:48,600
Wild chrysanthemum and mint?

68
00:03:49,590 --> 00:03:50,430
On my way here,

69
00:03:50,430 --> 00:03:51,360
the woods were full of them.

70
00:03:51,360 --> 00:03:52,160
I saw them myself.

71
00:03:52,430 --> 00:03:52,790
All right.

72
00:03:52,910 --> 00:03:53,760
Then I'll go with you.

73
00:03:53,960 --> 00:03:54,630
Oh, forget it.

74
00:03:54,630 --> 00:03:55,580
You can barely walk properly.

75
00:03:55,580 --> 00:03:56,410
How are you going to come with me?

76
00:03:56,410 --> 00:03:57,360
I can go on my own.

77
00:03:57,680 --> 00:03:58,680
Just stay home and rest.

78
00:03:58,680 --> 00:03:59,480
Then be careful.

79
00:03:59,910 --> 00:04:00,390
Okay.

80
00:04:05,870 --> 00:04:06,600
Mwah!

81
00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:10,950
Some sword wound, huh?

82
00:04:13,310 --> 00:04:14,550
See? You can't manage without me.

83
00:04:35,950 --> 00:04:37,150
Oh my goodness.

84
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:38,880
Good thing I have a secret advantage.

85
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:40,680
Now Shen Cheng's poison

86
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:41,880
should finally be curable.

87
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:48,120
Are you people out of your minds?

88
00:04:48,510 --> 00:04:49,440
Are you addicted to kidnapping?

89
00:04:49,720 --> 00:04:51,560
You think that little sedative
can knock me out?

90
00:04:51,680 --> 00:04:53,350
I practically eat
sleeping pills like candy.

91
00:04:53,630 --> 00:04:54,200
Wow.

92
00:04:55,800 --> 00:04:57,480
This is the first time I've heard

93
00:04:57,480 --> 00:04:59,200
a minor character talk
like that in a novel.

94
00:05:01,830 --> 00:05:02,320
Wait.

95
00:05:04,070 --> 00:05:04,830
Shutiao?

96
00:05:08,120 --> 00:05:08,760
Shutiao!

97
00:05:18,240 --> 00:05:19,080
Was I

98
00:05:20,510 --> 00:05:21,510
too impulsive?

99
00:05:21,720 --> 00:05:22,240
Oh, man.

100
00:05:22,240 --> 00:05:23,560
Shen He...

101
00:05:23,870 --> 00:05:25,360
You call yourself a traditional man,

102
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:26,430
yet you couldn't control yourself.

103
00:05:26,430 --> 00:05:26,800
Oh, man.

104
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:28,390
No.

105
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:31,560
I really need
to explain things properly.

106
00:05:33,040 --> 00:05:33,510
Shutiao.

107
00:05:54,750 --> 00:05:55,350
Third Madam.

108
00:05:56,040 --> 00:05:56,510
We

109
00:05:56,870 --> 00:05:57,710
meet again.

110
00:05:59,510 --> 00:06:00,210
You were the one

111
00:06:00,210 --> 00:06:01,560
who kidnapped us during
the estate inspection, weren't you?

112
00:06:02,270 --> 00:06:03,270
What exactly do you want?

113
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:04,640
You're quite clever.

114
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:06,640
I

115
00:06:07,360 --> 00:06:08,390
want money.

116
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:09,560
And you're

117
00:06:10,240 --> 00:06:11,950
worth a great deal of money.

118
00:06:12,360 --> 00:06:13,000
Fine.

119
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:14,390
Let me go,

120
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:16,030
and I'll pay you double the ransom.

121
00:06:16,310 --> 00:06:17,830
You're certainly
straightforward, Third Madam.

122
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:19,240
But

123
00:06:20,160 --> 00:06:21,760
I've just thought of another way.

124
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:24,000
A way

125
00:06:25,160 --> 00:06:26,390
to make the Third Young Master

126
00:06:26,750 --> 00:06:28,200
and even the entire Marquis's Manor

127
00:06:29,950 --> 00:06:32,080
keep paying me indefinitely.

128
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:34,200
You're worth

129
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:35,710
far more than silver.

130
00:06:37,560 --> 00:06:38,680
If you hurt me,

131
00:06:39,270 --> 00:06:40,570
the Marquis's Manor won't
let you get away with it.

132
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:42,910
The Marquis's Manor?

133
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:44,920
Surely you don't expect

134
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:46,480
that playboy who spends
all day at brothels

135
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:47,510
to risk his life saving you?

136
00:06:52,240 --> 00:06:53,880
You're only half right.

137
00:06:54,430 --> 00:06:55,080
What?

138
00:06:55,310 --> 00:06:56,390
Maybe no one

139
00:06:56,390 --> 00:06:57,310
in the Marquis's Manor

140
00:06:57,310 --> 00:06:58,470
would risk their life to save me.

141
00:06:59,270 --> 00:07:00,390
But there's one person

142
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:01,830
who would come for me.

143
00:07:03,070 --> 00:07:05,270
She's the family I chose for myself.

144
00:07:20,920 --> 00:07:21,510
Let her go!

145
00:07:24,680 --> 00:07:25,910
I'm warning you.

146
00:07:26,630 --> 00:07:27,260
When I swing this ax,

147
00:07:27,260 --> 00:07:27,960
it really hurts.

148
00:07:27,960 --> 00:07:28,600
Really hurts.

149
00:07:28,600 --> 00:07:29,910
Really, really hurts.

150
00:07:40,040 --> 00:07:40,830
You think you can scare me?

151
00:07:41,510 --> 00:07:42,150
I don't believe

152
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:44,080
the Wife of the Marquis's Heir

153
00:07:44,410 --> 00:07:45,130
would dare kill anyone.

154
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:46,760
You're right.

155
00:07:47,340 --> 00:07:48,350
I wouldn't dare kill anyone.

156
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:49,710
But

157
00:07:54,630 --> 00:07:56,190
I can make sure you

158
00:07:56,190 --> 00:07:57,120
never have children.

159
00:07:57,430 --> 00:07:58,870
For a monster like you,

160
00:07:58,870 --> 00:08:00,070
one swing of this ax

161
00:08:00,070 --> 00:08:00,920
will settle everything

162
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:02,120
once and for all.

163
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:21,080
Are you all right?

164
00:08:21,270 --> 00:08:21,800
I'm fine.

165
00:08:28,510 --> 00:08:29,350
I'm sorry.

166
00:08:29,620 --> 00:08:30,750
I had no choice.

167
00:08:30,870 --> 00:08:31,510
If I didn't help him,

168
00:08:31,510 --> 00:08:32,560
he'd ruin my life.

169
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:33,870
What...

170
00:08:34,480 --> 00:08:35,400
A useless teammate.

171
00:08:36,870 --> 00:08:38,150
Where's Third Madam?

172
00:08:38,360 --> 00:08:38,880
- Tell us.
- Tell us.

173
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:39,770
We were just

174
00:08:39,960 --> 00:08:41,300
paid to do the job.

175
00:08:41,300 --> 00:08:42,520
Who put you up to this?

176
00:08:42,620 --> 00:08:43,100
It was...

177
00:08:43,230 --> 00:08:44,630
It was Pei Qian.

178
00:08:44,870 --> 00:08:45,720
He told us

179
00:08:45,860 --> 00:08:47,990
to kidnap Her Ladyship and Third Madam.

180
00:09:06,720 --> 00:09:08,160
As expected of a lady
of the Marquis's Manor.

181
00:09:09,360 --> 00:09:10,920
Just look at your delicate skin.

182
00:09:11,750 --> 00:09:13,520
If I painted a portrait of you,

183
00:09:14,480 --> 00:09:15,440
it would be worth far more

184
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:17,400
than those ordinary beauties out there.

185
00:09:19,530 --> 00:09:20,210
Have you lost your mind?

186
00:09:20,550 --> 00:09:21,990
You only said
we'd kidnap them for ransom.

187
00:09:22,050 --> 00:09:23,450
You never mentioned making
those kinds of paintings.

188
00:09:23,630 --> 00:09:24,320
What do you know?

189
00:09:24,960 --> 00:09:25,800
Once a woman

190
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:27,630
has such a portrait painted

191
00:09:28,270 --> 00:09:29,200
and I have it in my possession,

192
00:09:30,150 --> 00:09:32,110
she'll be at my mercy for life,

193
00:09:32,550 --> 00:09:33,680
paying me again and again.

194
00:09:34,440 --> 00:09:35,550
That's much easier

195
00:09:35,550 --> 00:09:36,920
than kidnapping.

196
00:09:39,150 --> 00:09:40,040
Isn't that exactly

197
00:09:40,840 --> 00:09:41,480
why you've

198
00:09:41,480 --> 00:09:43,040
always obeyed my every word?

199
00:09:50,960 --> 00:09:51,870
It's a fine painting, isn't it?

200
00:09:52,240 --> 00:09:53,710
Even more alluring
than you are in person.

201
00:09:54,630 --> 00:09:55,320
Five hundred taels.

202
00:09:55,750 --> 00:09:56,560
Otherwise, tomorrow,

203
00:09:56,750 --> 00:09:58,040
I'll put it up for public sale.

204
00:09:58,390 --> 00:09:59,590
You clearly told me

205
00:10:00,030 --> 00:10:01,710
you only painted it
for our private enjoyment.

206
00:10:02,510 --> 00:10:03,950
You promised never to show anyone.

207
00:10:07,030 --> 00:10:08,350
As long as you obey me,

208
00:10:08,790 --> 00:10:09,320
I'll make sure

209
00:10:09,670 --> 00:10:11,080
this painting stays safely hidden.

210
00:10:11,720 --> 00:10:12,920
But if you disobey me,

211
00:10:13,910 --> 00:10:16,320
I'll let everyone in the capital see

212
00:10:16,510 --> 00:10:17,440
just what kind of

213
00:10:17,790 --> 00:10:18,440
shameless woman

214
00:10:18,440 --> 00:10:19,710
the Marquis's adopted daughter
really is.

215
00:10:20,550 --> 00:10:21,280
You were the one who said

216
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:23,280
refusing to pose meant
I didn't love you.

217
00:10:23,670 --> 00:10:24,920
I only let you paint me
because I loved you.

218
00:10:26,790 --> 00:10:27,750
And I painted you

219
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:29,320
because I love you too.

220
00:10:31,270 --> 00:10:32,160
Then let them go.

221
00:10:32,480 --> 00:10:33,440
You promised me.

222
00:10:34,120 --> 00:10:34,840
You only kidnapped them

223
00:10:34,840 --> 00:10:36,320
to pay off your gambling debts.

224
00:10:36,750 --> 00:10:38,040
If you make those paintings of them,

225
00:10:38,670 --> 00:10:39,870
their reputations will be ruined.

226
00:10:40,320 --> 00:10:40,950
Not a chance.

227
00:10:41,750 --> 00:10:43,240
With two such valuable sources of money,

228
00:10:43,240 --> 00:10:43,950
why would I let them go?

229
00:10:49,240 --> 00:10:49,590
Please don't.

230
00:10:50,270 --> 00:10:50,750
I'm begging you.

231
00:10:51,200 --> 00:10:52,200
Please let them go.

232
00:10:52,440 --> 00:10:53,590
Whatever you want, I'll find the money.

233
00:10:54,670 --> 00:10:55,470
Just let them go.

234
00:10:55,670 --> 00:10:56,280
Get out of my way!

235
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:09,820
♪No matter how
the universe changes tomorrow♪

236
00:11:09,820 --> 00:11:17,020
♪Right now,
I just want to stay by your side♪

237
00:11:17,020 --> 00:11:22,220
♪Let this kiss and this dream
last until we're old♪

238
00:11:23,420 --> 00:11:28,460
♪And hold on to all
the tenderness of this moment♪

239
00:11:29,820 --> 00:11:34,900
♪Following this heartbeat,
we'll retrace our steps♪

240
00:11:36,260 --> 00:11:41,380
♪As time goes by,
all I need is your gaze♪

241
00:11:42,660 --> 00:11:46,020
♪One dream until our hair turns gray♪

242
00:12:04,780 --> 00:12:08,140
♪One dream until our hair turns gray♪
